# Moore's Voting Algorithm

## 1. Trigger Clues
- Find an element appearing **more than n/2 times**.
- Need O(n) time and O(1) extra space.

## 2. Core Intuition
Cancel pairs of different elements. Since the majority element appears more times than all other elements combined, it cannot be completely cancelled.

## 3. Java Template
```java
int count = 0, ele = 0;

for (int num : nums) {
    if (count == 0) {
        ele = num;
        count = 1;
    } else if (num == ele) {
        count++;
    } else {
        count--;
    }
}

return ele;
```

*Assumes a majority element exists.*

## 4. Complexity
- **Time:** O(n)
- **Auxiliary Space:** O(1)

## 5. Common Mistakes
- Treating the candidate as confirmed when a majority is not guaranteed.
- Forgetting to verify the candidate with a second pass when necessary.
- Confusing this with Majority Element II (more than n/3), which requires two candidates.

